NAME
    load - write a raw file's bytes into a memory space

SYNOPSIS
    load <space> <addr> <file>

DESCRIPTION
    Reads raw bytes from <file> (for example, a file produced by dump(1))
    and writes them into memory space <space> starting at hex <addr>.
    Refuses read-only memory spaces (see spaces(1)).

    Relative <file> paths resolve under /Logs/<CoreName>/; paths starting
    with '/' resolve from the shell sandbox root (see hier(7)). Paths that
    escape the sandbox root are refused.

EXAMPLES
    load WRAM 0 wram.bin
    load WRAM 0 /Logs/wram.bin

EXIT STATUS
    0   Bytes loaded (or usage/refusal/not-found message printed).
    1   Path outside sandbox, no target attached, invalid hex argument,
        or I/O or session service fault.

SEE ALSO
    dump(1), write(1), mem(1), spaces(1), hier(7)
